# Environment Variable Configuration Template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' in this project directory: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Replace the placeholder values below with your own valid values.
# 3. NEVER commit your actual '.env' file or any real secrets to Git.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Demo application (fixtures/demo-app) ---
# PORT=4000

# --- Browser runtime ---
# Point to a pre-installed Chromium binary instead of the one `npx playwright
# install chromium` downloads (useful in CI images/sandboxes with a browser
# already baked in, or restricted network egress).
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium

# --- Where runs are written (CLI and MCP server must agree on this) ---
# QA_ARTIFACTS_DIR=./artifacts
# Retention, applied after every run. Only UUID-named run directories are deleted. 0 disables a limit.
# QA_ARTIFACTS_MAX_RUNS=50
# QA_ARTIFACTS_MAX_AGE_DAYS=7

# --- Security / target policy ---
# Deterministic test execution (src/runner, src/assertions) needs no API key.
# Local-dev opt-in is a CLI flag (--allow-local-dev) or MCP tool argument
# (allowLocalDev) only - there is no environment variable for it, so a test
# run's security posture is always explicit at the call site.

# --- Optional AI planner / diagnosis (plan_qa_test, get_failure_evidence diagnose:true) ---
# Set at most one of these two keys, or set LLM_PROVIDER to pick between them
# if both happen to be set. See README "AI Planner: Model & Pricing Choice".
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
